    {
      "id": "HCAP-14",
      "name": "live NFSv4.1 session BIND transport reset",
      "purpose": "Drive a fresh NFSv4.1 client and session from the program on a client0 lane transport, then pipeline BIND_CONN_TO_SESSION on that transport and reset it",
      "usable_stage": [
        "stage1"
      ],
      "usable_by": [
        "agent_stage1"
      ],
      "interface": {
        "syz_calls": [
          "recvfrom$inet_nfs_fuzz_tcp",
          "recvfrom$nfs41_create_session",
          "recvfrom$nfs41_exchange_id",
          "setsockopt$sock_linger",
          "syz_open_nfs_lane_profile$client0_knfsd_v41",
          "syz_socket_connect_nfs_lane$client0_knfsd_v41",
          "write$nfs41_bind_conn_to_session",
          "write$nfs41_create_session",
          "write$nfs41_exchange_id"
        ]
      },
      "constraints": [
        "one non-threaded Stage 1 program on client0; syz_socket_connect_nfs_lane takes the exact client0 knfsd-v41 profile directory fd as its lane token and only opens the TCP transport, with 3 s send/receive timeouts",
        "the program writes each one-op COMPOUND itself: EXCHANGE_ID, then CREATE_SESSION with the clientid and sequenceid that recvfrom$nfs41_exchange_id captured, then one write of 1..64 BIND_CONN_TO_SESSION records with the sessionid that recvfrom$nfs41_create_session captured",
        "requests use an empty tag and AUTH_SYS so the first op result sits 48 bytes into the reply record; a failed op leaves the captured resources meaningless and the later calls fail",
        "dir 3 (FORE_OR_BOTH) reaches the cn_flags read-modify-write path; one round is connect, the six session calls, a zero setsockopt$sock_linger and close; a program holds at most 4 rounds (syzkaller's 40-call limit), so more rounds come from repeated execution",
        "client owners are fixed program bytes, so a repeated program reuses its confirmed client within the lease and opens a new session on it",
        "direct knfsd endpoint; the profile acquisition is parser-proven, the socket inherits its origin, and the calls cannot be used without it",
        "this capability establishes live-session BIND and transport-reset reachability, not a race outcome or KASAN"
      ],
      "status": "experimental",
      "scope": [
        "live_bind_transport_reset"
      ],
      "validated_scope": [],
      "source_refs": [
        "bundle/patches/syzkaller/0031-*",
        "env/syzkaller/sys/linux/socket_inet_nfs.txt",
        "stage1-host-live/live-bind.syz",
        "stage1-host-live/live-bind-race.syz",
        "stage1-host-live/live-bind-race64p.syz"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "HCAP-15",
      "name": "live NFSv4.1 session RECLAIM_COMPLETE",
      "purpose": "Drive SEQUENCE followed by RECLAIM_COMPLETE on a live NFSv4.1 session created by the program on the client0 lane transport",
      "usable_stage": [
        "stage1"
      ],
      "usable_by": [
        "agent_stage1"
      ],
      "interface": {
        "syz_calls": [
          "recvfrom$nfs41_reclaim_complete",
          "write$nfs41_reclaim_complete"
        ]
      },
      "constraints": [
        "requires the exact contiguous open, connect, EXCHANGE_ID write/read, CREATE_SESSION write/read and RECLAIM_COMPLETE write/read chain on the same client0 knfsd-v41 TCP transport; reply resources provide the client ID, sequence ID and session ID consumed by later requests",
        "EXCHANGE_ID, CREATE_SESSION and RECLAIM_COMPLETE use the same fixed AUTH_SYS principal with empty machine name, uid 0, gid 0 and no supplementary groups",
        "EXCHANGE_ID and CREATE_SESSION flags are zero; both CREATE_SESSION channels use headerpad 0, request and response size 4096, cached response size 0, maxops 8, maxreqs 4 and no RDMA attributes",
        "the typed call emits a two-operation NFSv4.1 COMPOUND with SEQUENCE first and RECLAIM_COMPLETE second; sequence ID 1, slot 0, highest slot 0 and cachethis false are protocol-fixed",
        "all three request writes are no-squash typed structures, and generated, parsed and mutated programs must preserve these bootstrap conditions; the final typed receive is the response and remote-coverage barrier",
        "direct knfsd endpoint; the socket resource must originate from nfs-profile:knfsd-v41:client0",
        "this capability establishes live-session RECLAIM_COMPLETE reachability and does not claim a crash outcome"
      ],
      "status": "experimental",
      "scope": [
        "live_reclaim_complete"
      ],
      "validated_scope": [],
      "source_refs": [
        "bundle/patches/syzkaller/0040-*",
        "fs/nfsd/nfs4state.c:nfsd4_reclaim_complete"
      ],
      "fills_gap": "nfs41.reclaim_complete.session_call",
      "contract": {
        "entry_points": [
          {
            "kind": "syz_call",
            "name": "write$nfs41_reclaim_complete"
          }
        ],
        "boundary_functions": [
          "nfsd4_reclaim_complete"
        ],
        "fixed_types": [
          "rpc_tcp_nfs41_compound2_record_t"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
